Mangayomi — https://github.com/kodjodevf/mangayomi
Apache License 2.0 — full text in licenses/Mangayomi-Apache-2.0.txt

  Most of `lib/source/` is the Mangayomi extension runtime: the d4rt bridge and
  its registered classes, the source models (`MManga`, `MChapter`, `MPages`,
  `MSource`, filters, documents, elements), the HTTP client, the DOM and
  regular-expression helpers, and the crypto utilities.

  MODIFICATIONS. Per section 4(b) of the Apache License, this is notice that
  files in `lib/source/` have been changed from their upstream originals. The
  changes are deliberately few, because published extensions are written
  against upstream behaviour. They are:

    - `kBridgeLibraryUri` is a named constant rather than a literal. It still
      resolves to `package:mangayomi/bridge_lib.dart`, which is the URI every
      published extension imports, and must not be renamed.
    - Quote style, to satisfy this project's formatter.
    - Date-locale data is initialised before the first parse
      (`MBridge._ensureDateFormatting`), where upstream initialises only
      inside its fallback loop.
    - Relative links are resolved once, in `DartSourceRuntime._absolute`.
    - Source preferences are read lazily and never seeded, where upstream
      writes a copy on first read.

  Several files — `m_manga.dart` among them — are byte-identical to upstream.
  `CLAUDE.md` records which, and why diffing against upstream must precede any
  change to this tree.

